From 3c6bddb383b219d4aa51152914b988462cb9be0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:38:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] DJ booth: dual CDJ decks + two-channel mixer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Booth: two CDJ-style decks side by side with a mixer between them
- per deck: LCD (title, PLAYING/PAUSED, elapsed / remaining, BPM x tempo),
  needle-search strip with hot-cue and cue marks, jog wheel (VINYL: scratch,
  off: search), CUE (CDJ behaviour) + PLAY/PAUSE, hot cues A-D, tempo fader
  ±8/±16/wide, TAP tempo, SYNC, 5 s skips
- mixer: channel faders with level meters, crossfader (MIX/CUT curves),
  master, audio/video output, FX pads aimed at the on-air deck
- crate: paste a link → LOAD 1 / LOAD 2 / + CRATE; crate items load to
  either deck; loop + now-playing strip options
- keys: Z/X deck 1 cue/play, N/M deck 2, 1-4 / 7-0 hot cues, arrows xfade

Server: deck B under media['b']; every deck action takes 'deck';
mix, cue_main, cue_return, bpm, sync, duration, load_queued; dj_fx carries
the deck. Deck A stays top-level so the queue and older clients still work.

Projector: two YouTube players; volume = master x channel x crossfader
curve; in video mode deck B's picture fades over deck A with the
crossfader; reports track length; FX duck/brake only the deck they target.
